From 6432f7d46c14dee5d15ab650de6e368425edf59b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:07:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 58/82] sunxi: h713: hy300_pro_defconfig, the HY300 Pro's own
 board base

The HY300 Pro (issue #1) had no base of its own: boards/hy300-pro/uboot.config
carried its DRAM block but named the bench board's device tree and said so in a
comment, because the fragment was only ever meant for a probe build. Stage 5
wants a test image for that board, and a test image needs a base.

It is hy310_defconfig with three things changed, and nothing else, because
nothing else has been measured as different: the DRAM block is this board's own
24 words (its vendor boot0 at LBA 16, printed by h713_probe on the owner's
device and confirmed against his full dump), the clock is his 636 MHz instead
of the HY310's 792, and the device tree and identification string name the
board. Against the HY310 that is the clock, tpr11/tpr12 (0x44440000/0x00005555
rather than 0x44340000/0x00006666) and the two of tpr0..tpr2 the DDR3 path
recomputes from the clock anyway.

No image is shipped from this base. The board is below `verified` -- its owner
has run the installer in dump-only mode and nothing else -- so the only build
it is meant for is the stage 5 test image, built on purpose and flashed by that
owner alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 configs/hy300_pro_defconfig | 102 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 102 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 configs/hy300_pro_defconfig

diff --git a/configs/hy300_pro_defconfig b/configs/hy300_pro_defconfig
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..538ecd598a8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/configs/hy300_pro_defconfig
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+# HY300 Pro -- board base. Reported in issue #1 by its owner (GitHub
+# `fightforlife`); nobody here has ever held this board.
+#
+# Same shape as hy310_defconfig: this file says what the hardware is, a role
+# fragment in configs/fragments/ says what a build is for, and
+# build/uboot-build.sh merges the two (docs/uboot/README.md, "Which
+# defconfig"). Everything outside the DRAM block, the device tree name and the
+# identification string is the HY310 base, unchanged -- the two boards are the
+# same SoC, the same eMMC size, the same console, and no difference between
+# them has been measured anywhere else.
+#
+# **No image is shipped for this board.** It is below `verified`
+# (boards/hy300-pro/README.md, boards/README.md honesty rule): its owner has
+# run our installer in dump-only mode and nothing else. The only build this
+# base is meant for is the stage 5 *test image*, built on purpose
+# (`--test-image`), named `-TEST`, and flashed by that owner alone.
+#
+# Where the values come from:
+#   - the DRAM block below is boards/hy300-pro/uboot.config verbatim: the 24
+#     words of this board's own vendor boot0 at LBA 16, printed by h713_probe
+#     on the owner's device and confirmed against his dd of the full dump
+#     (issue #1, 2026-09-14). Nothing in it is borrowed.
+#   - CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=636 is his boot0's own clock, and his UART log agrees
+#     (`DRAM CLK = 636 MHz`, `Type = 3`, `SIZE = 1024 M`). It is *not* the
+#     HY310's 792: our installer SPL trained his board at 792 for a 17-minute
+#     dump, which proves "enough for a dump", not "stable in operation".
+#   - tpr11/tpr12 0x44440000/0x00005555 are this board's, and differ from the
+#     HY310's 0x44340000/0x00006666.
+#   - tpr0..tpr2 are in the file for completeness only; the DDR3 path in
+#     arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50iw12.c recomputes them from CONFIG_DRAM_CLK
+#     and overwrites whatever is configured here.
+#   - para2 and tpr13 are the values the vendor flash tool writes, as on a
+#     device.
+#   - the device tree is sun50i-h713-hy300-pro, an include of the bench board's
+#     plus model and compatible -- the same pattern as the HY310's. The panel
+#     is not described there by anyone: it comes through the display
+#     coprocessor's own tables. This board's panel is unknown beyond its
+#     declared project id 0x34.
+CONFIG_ARM=y
+CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI=y
+CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE="allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro"
+CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=636
+CONFIG_SPL=y
+CONFIG_IDENT_STRING=" HY300 Pro"
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_DX_ODT=0x03030303
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_DX_DRI=0x0e0e0e0e
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_CA_DRI=0x1c12
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_ODT_EN=0x1
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_ZQ=0x007b7bfb
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_PARA1=0x000010f4
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_PARA2=0x04000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_MR0=0x00001c70
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_MR1=0x00000040
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_MR2=0x00000018
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_MR3=0x00000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR0=0x00482151
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR1=0x01b1a94d
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR2=0x0007004e
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR3=0xb4787896
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR4=0x00000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR5=0x48484848
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR6=0x00000048
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR7=0x1620121e
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR8=0x00000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR9=0x00000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR10=0x00000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR11=0x44440000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR12=0x00005555
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR13=0xb4016103
+CONFIG_MACH_SUN50I_H713=y
+CONFIG_H713_POWERON_LIGHT_FAN=y
+CONFIG_H713_MIPS_BOOT=y
+CONFIG_SUNXI_DRAM_H713_DDR3_STOCK=y
+CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA=2
+CONFIG_MMC0_CD_PIN=""
+# CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_CLEAR_ON_INIT is not set
+CONFIG_SUPPORT_EMMC_BOOT=y
+CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
+CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
+# CONFIG_WATCHDOG is not set
+CONFIG_WDT=y
+CONFIG_USB_MUSB_GADGET=y
+CONFIG_CMD_USB_MASS_STORAGE=y
+# CONFIG_USB_ETHER is not set
+CONFIG_CONSOLE_MUX=y
+CONFIG_SYS_CONSOLE_IS_IN_ENV=y
+CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_ACM=y
+# CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_ACM_WAIT_FOR_CONNECTION is not set
+CONFIG_SYSRESET=y
+CONFIG_SYSRESET_PSCI=y
+CONFIG_CMD_POWEROFF=y
+CONFIG_FASTBOOT_CMD_OEM_POWEROFF=y
+CONFIG_PREBOOT="if itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xfa57b007; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; run fastboot_mode; elif itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xb007c0de; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; setenv bootdelay -1; fi; usb start"
+# CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT is not set
+CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC=y
+CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET=0x700000
+CONFIG_ENV_MMC_DEVICE_INDEX=1
+CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR=0x800
+CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_DATA_PART_OFFSET=0x0
+CONFIG_H713_VENDOR_CHAINLOAD=y
+CONFIG_CMD_WDT=y
+CONFIG_CMD_GPIO=y
